        "policy": "Income - Government Child Care benefits",
        "description": "* Canada Child Benefit (CCB) income as well as applicable Provincial benefits may be considered provided the following is obtained:\r\n* CCB statement\r\n* Confirmation of child\u2019s date of birth by copy of birth certificate if CCB statement does not specify the age of the child.\r\n* 3 month bank statement showing deposit history\r\n* The following conditions apply:\r\n* Exclude any income from children who turn age 13 or older in the calendar year from the total. As the CCB statement does not specify the amount per child, use the appropriate percentage for the number of children age 12 and under.  \r\n* Primary residence only",
