        "description": "All pensions are to be permanent income. The following are **acceptable** pension types:\r\n- Public: Federal and or Provincial programs (i.e. CPP, QPP, OAS)\r\n- Income derived from the federal Guaranteed Income Supplement program is not eligible\r\n- Employer: Canadian Company or Government Employee pension\r\n- Foreign: Foreign pensions that are paid into a Canadian bank account and income is declared and taxed in Canada\r\n\r\n**Documentation Requirements:**\r\nThe amount of pension income being used is to be reasonable and verified as follows:\r\n- Public (CPP, QPP, OAS): One of the following confirming pension income:\r\n- Most recent T4A slip(s)\r\n- Most recent NOA and corresponding T1 General\r\n- Recent bank statement/pension stub to show at least one direct deposit to applicants account\r\n- Borrowers receiving OAS pension: if the applicant\u2019s income exceeds $77,580, the OAS pension is subject to claw back therefore current/ongoing eligibility verification is required if being used to qualify.\r\n\r\nEmployer: Any two of the following confirming pension income:\r\n- A recent pension statement/stub or bank statement to show direct deposit dated within 30 days\r\n- Most recent T4A\r\n- Most recent NOA supported by the T1 General\r\n- A letter from the previous employer/pension administrator confirming the pension amount\r\n\r\nForeign:\r\n- A recent pension statement/stub or bank statement to show direct deposit dated within 30 days as well as the most recent two years NOAs supported by the T1 Generals.",
