        "policy": "Income - Salaried, Hourly, Contract, Part-Time, Bonus or Casual",
        "description": "* LOE & pay stub \r\n\r\nPart Time Income;\r\n* The options for verifying part time income and employment are being streamlined to simplify requirements and ensure a 2 year history is obtained.  \r\n* A letter from the employer that confirms permanent part time status, hours and current income is an acceptable form of secondary verification.  The letter must confirm earnings for the last two years.   \r\n\r\nOvertime/shift premiums/shift differential/living allowance\r\n*  A 2 year history has to be established if using. \r\n* We will use the lower of the 2 year average or income from the most recent year\r\n* 2 years NOAs required as above or T4s depending on what the eligible income is.\r\n\r\nBonus income \r\n* 2 years T4s are required\r\n* will use 50% of the average of the bonus income earned in the last 2 years or 50% of the bonus earned for the most recent year, which ever is less.\r\n* The last paystub/notification of direct deposit is acceptable in place of a T4.\r\n* If using a 2 year average for income only need to confirm taxes owing on most recent year above $2500.  if under this amount do not need to provide confirmation of paid.",
