        "description": "**Documentation Requirements**\r\n\r\n**Rental Income Verification**\r\n* You must verify rental income using one of the following methods:\r\n* CRA Documents:\r\n* Notice of Assessment (or CRA \"My Account\" Income Statement)\r\n* Matching T1 General, including Statement of Real Estate Rentals\r\n* Must be from the most recent tax year\r\n* Appraisal Documents:\r\n* Full appraisal report with Market Rent Estimate\r\n* OR Schedule A from a Scotiabank-approved appraiser\r\n* Lease Agreements + Bank Statements:\r\n* Copies of current leases\r\n* Supported by three consecutive months of bank statements\r\n\r\n**Exception**\r\n\r\n* For purchase transactions with existing tenants, leases alone are acceptable \u2014 bank statements are not required.\r\n\r\n**For Existing Rental Properties Owned by the Borrower**\r\n\r\n* Only the following are accepted:\r\n* Leases, or\r\n* CRA documentation\r\n* Appraisals or Schedule A documents are NOT acceptable for this purpose.\r\n\r\n**Additional Notes**\r\n\r\n* For non-subject rental properties, income must be calculated using the Broker Form: Rental Analysis Worksheet, available under the \u2018Forms\u2019 tab on scotiamortgageauthority.com",
