        "id": 117,
        "policy": "APV (Auto Property Valuation)",
        "description": "For some applications, an appraisal report may not be required based on Scotiabank Policy. The CMHC Property Assessment Tool (PAT) may be used to confirm value in the following circumstances:\r\n* Owner occupied principal residence\r\n* Property Value is less than $1,250,000 (GTA/GVA), $1,000,000 Rest of ON/BC or less than $750,000 in all other regions\r\n* MLS purchase or switch (no additional funds) with an LTV equal to or less than 80%\r\n* Refinance (including switch with additional funds) with an LTV of 75% or less for properties owned for more than 12 months\r\n* New construction completion properties submitted with a full municipal address and postal code, submitted with a purchase agreement, property details and an approved new home warranty.\r\n* Standard application (no specialty programs, including StartRight, etc).\r\n* The cost of PAT is $100.00 if the property value is accepted. No further verification of value is required if the PAT application is successful. If a Flex (desktop) like appraisal is required, the fee will now be $300.\r\n\r\n\r\n**FCT**\r\n* Partnership available for auto-evaluations \r\n* Allows BRM/BLM to attempt to verify property values without requiring an appraisal for many types of applications, including refinances\r\n* Some restrictions apply\r\n* Please be advised that effective Monday February 28th 2022, Non-Owner-Occupied Rentals/Investment Properties will no longer be eligible for an auto-valuation, and Scotiabank\u2019s existing valuations requirements of a full appraisal will now be required for all rental properties.\r\n* Please also note that if a valuation is received through FCT on eligible properties, a resubmission is now required to FCT to be reassessed to confirm application is still eligible for valuation when material changes are made.  Please note that when making a change to any application, it could impact whether we the valuation is still valid or not.  The system will be using algorithms other than property value such as credit rating, income, overall deal strength. \r\n* For eligible transactions, only the 3 material changes listed below will require a resubmission for FCT.  There are no exceptions to this.\r\n* An increase in purchase price or declared value\r\n* An increase in loan amount.",
        "isAccepted": 1
