        "description": "* The loan is to be by way of short term unsecured demand loan for a maximum term of 3 months, tied to the closing date of the property being sold by the borrower.\r\n* Interest only is accrued monthly and payable when the loan is repaid.\r\n* The bridge loan amount together with the mortgage amount on the new property cannot exceed the purchase price of the new property being bought. Legals and land transfer costs may be added to this calculation if the bridge loan amount including the legals and land transfer costs does not exceed net sale proceeds of the property for sale.\r\n* The bridge loan is for a period of no longer than 90 days following the closing date of the new property being purchased.\r\n\r\nDebt Servicing\r\n* If a bridge loan was for a longer period, then the insurer would require that the bridge loan be included in the TDS calculation. In the event that the bridge loan is not expected to be repaid within 90 days, then 3% of the loan principal is to be included in the TDS calculation.\r\n* Approval for the combined financing exposure of the bridge loan and other MBC facilities (which may also include interim financing as detailed in Section 11.3) is to be obtained from a credit approver with the appropriate DLA.\r\n\r\nSecurity\r\n* Letter of Direction and Undertaking to Pay re proceeds on sale of existing property\r\n* Full personal guarantees\r\n* Independent Legal Advice where appropriate.\r\n* Undertaking to provide a mortgage on the existing property (if one is not already in place) if the saleas anticipated falls through for the full amount of the bridge loan.\r\n\r\n**Fee**\r\n\r\nPrime plus 2.00%\r\nA $500 fee applies to all Bridge Financing. It is available for clients who are opening a Manulife bank Mortgage only",
