        "policy": "Income - Child & Spousal Support",
        "description": "* Income is to only represent < 50% of the total gross income being used to qualify.\r\n* Exceptions: Insured and Insurable loans on case by case base only\r\n\r\n**Documentation Requirements**\r\n* Fully executed court order or separation agreement signed by both parties and executed by lawyer/notary\r\n* In situations where a court order or separation agreement is not attainable, receipt of Statutory Declaration or Affidavit (witnessed by a solicitor/notary) to be provided.\r\n* Both required to be supported with the most recently filed T1 General or bank statements showing 3 recent consecutive months history\r\n\r\n**For Support Payable**\r\n* If the Borrower is responsible for Alimony/Child support, the payment amount of Alimony/Child support is to be included in the Borrower's liabilities.\r\n\r\n**Documentation Requirements**\r\n* Fully executed court order or separation agreement signed by both parties and executed by lawyer/notary.\r\n- Separation Agreement:\r\n   - Does not need to be notarized, just witnessed by a 3rd party. \r\n   - In the case of spousal separation, whether the borrowers are married or common-law, the finalized separation agreement or court order signed by both parties and witnessed by a third party or executed by a lawyer/notary is always required to confirm the details of any child support/alimony payments",
