        "id": 496,
        "policy": "Income - Investments",
        "description": "The 2-year average must be used provided:\r\n\r\n* Investment is not being liquidated (i.e.; used for the down payment)\r\n* Income is not from capital gains\r\n* Income used does not exceed 5% of the total remaining investments\r\n* Income is confirmed to continue at the same level or expected to increase\r\n* Where investment income is declining from one year to the next, the most recent year to be used\r\n* 50% of the income derived from a mortgage receivable can be used to qualify only if the mortgage receivable has been in place for a minimum of 2 years and will continue \r\n  for the term of the proposed mortgage.\r\n \r\nDocumentation Requirements\r\n\r\n* Investment Statements dated no more than 60 days of the application date\r\n* Most recent 2 years NOAs or T5s\r\n*  If the income is derived from a mortgage receivable:\r\n     Copy of the mortgage document confirming regular payments is required\r\n     Investment statement to reflect borrower name (first & last), investment company, account number, balances, be dated within 60 days of application date",
