        "policy": "Income - Other Taxable",
        "description": "**Car Allowance/Phone Allowance**\r\n- May now be added to qualifying income or used as an offset to car loan/lease payments. Applicable to taxable income only, with confirmation of funds being received.\r\n    - Documentation Requirements: Most recent T4 or current paystub identifying car allowance as taxable benefit\r\n\r\n**Living Allowance**\r\n* 2 year average can be used provided:\r\n* Does not exceed 25% of total income and is taxable\r\n* Rent paid by employer is only acceptable provided is a taxable benefit\r\n* Letter of employment confirming taxable living allowance\r\n* Most recent 2 years NOAs\r\n* Most recent paystub or 3 months history of direct deposits\r\n\r\n**RRIF, RRSP**\r\n* Income may be used provided the investment balance supports an annual draw for a minimum of 3 years.\r\n* A 2 year average is used as qualifying income provided all of the following:\r\n* RRSP/RRIF is not being liquidated ( i.e. used for down payment)\r\n* Income used does not exceed 5% of the total remaining amount\r\n* Income is  confirmed to continue at the same level or expected to increase\r\n* If the most recent year has declined over the previous by 10% or more, the most current year is to be used\r\n* Documentation Requirements\r\n* RRIF/RRSP statements (to support income for a minimum of 3 years) and 2 years T4s or NOAs to support\r\n* RRIF/RRSP statements to reflect Borrower name (first & last), investment company, account number, balances, to be dated within 60 days of application date\r\n\r\n**Fluctuating Income (e.g., Airbnb, Uber, Lyft, DoorDash)**\r\n- ***Airbnb***\r\n    - We don\u2019t take  type income at all. \r\n- ***For second job type income (ie. Uber, Door Dash)***\r\n    - We would treat that as part time so we would want to see a 2 year history of filed income. \r\n    - If there are large fluctuations between the years we would need to determine what income could be used.",
