        "policy": "Income - Salaried, Hourly, Contract, Part-Time, Bonus or Casual",
        "description": "**Salaried/Hourly Income**\r\n* Require any two sources of income verification via: \r\n* Employment letter dated within 60 days of application date AND\r\n     o Current pay stub dated within 60 days of application date AND/OR\r\n     o Most recent notice of assessment (NOA) (in certain cases an original signed T1013 from the client may be requested) AND/OR\r\n     o Recent bank statement showing at least two direct pay deposits.\r\n\r\n**Part-Time Income**\r\n* 100% of permanent part-time income, where hours are not guaranteed, will be considered if borrower can demonstrate a minimum 2-year history supported by Notices of Assessment or T4s. Lesser of 2-year average or most recent year\u2019s income.  Note: if part-time employment tenure is less than 2 years, we can consider if the employer confirms in writing that the client is required to work a minimum number of guaranteed hours per week. The minimum guaranteed \r\nweekly hours will be used to qualify.\r\n\r\n**Contract Income**\r\n* 100% of contract income can be used; for all transactions, we will require the following:\r\n\u2022 Employment contract and current pay stub. \r\n\u2022 Note: Contract must have a minimum of 6 months remaining from scheduled mortgage advance date or be renewing.\r\n\u2022 Bank statements confirming deposits are required if the client doesn\u2019t receive pay stubs. \r\n\u2022 If recently changes from salary to contract, use two-year history if in same line of work.\r\n\r\n**Variable Income**\r\n\u2022 If qualifying income includes variable income such as bonuses, overtime, etc. then two years\u2019 notices of assessment or T4\u2019s is required in addition to employment letter and either the most recent pay stub or bank statement. \r\n\u2022 During tax season (Jan-April), the lender will accept a prior year-end paystub in lieu of the most recent Notice of Assessment. The paystub must be third party such as Pay Works, Ceridian, or ADP.\"",
